  "reviewNotes": "Complete 20-entry lexical asset translated directly after inspecting installed Lexicon and every call site in full assembly decompilation. Child/adult gender suffixes select speaker vocabulary, not adjective agreement: PurchasedItem_5_Cooking applies those adjectives to Pierre as chef. All adjective variants use masculine singular; future Romanian caller clauses must use bucătar, miros, preparat or ceva. PurchasedItem_1 descriptions take adjective 3 for miros; PurchasedItem_3 uses adjective 4 for food and optional noun 5 for rubbish. NPC.cs.4135/.4138 must describe item as ceva before adjective 1. Child and pronoun forms match the already reviewed Chat_Baby; possessives match Chat_HouseUpgrade. All # alternatives remain in source order and none is empty. Editorial follow-up uses familiar fain for nifty and established vomitiv for sickening. For PurchasedItem_1, use Mirosea a ceva {3} în toată casa so every culinary adjective, including sățios, has a natural referent.",
